  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening governance and public service delivery in land and water resources tenure security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to significant political and administrative complexities, uncertainties surrounding land and water rights for Palestinians in the West Bank have led to the frequent inability to access water and land resources, which impacts their livelihoods. The involvement of Dutch expertise in the LAND-at-scale project brings substantial added value, particularly due to the Netherlands&apos; long-standing expertise in water and land governance. By focusing on government-to-government (G2G) capacity building, the project aims to modernise Palestinian state functions in several key areas, ultimately leading to better support for Palestinian farmers, to more Land and Water resources tenure security and the protection of their land. This will be established through tailor-made training and strengthening the technical capacity and public services for managing water and land matters in the Palestinian Territories.</narrative>
  </description>
